well as families across the valleys  really struggle to stay afloat a lot of  southern nevadans are  stepping in to help 8 news now reporter  kate houston shows us how one local  woman  turned her living room full of donations  into a full-blown  charity it's probably the single most  fulfilling thing outside of my own  motherhood that i've ever done  tammy dukey founded hope cove in may  after seeing so many families struggle  to feed  and care for their babies a teenage  momma and she had her  little baby with her and her baby was  wearing  hand to god paper towels wrapped in  cling wrap  for a diaper i cried for 20 minutes  after she left  initially dookie used her living room as  a central location  to collect donations from across the  valley what started as a few boxes  soon stacked to the ceiling it  snowballed it just grew and grew and  grew  soon we were bursting out of my house  hope cove has now expanded to its very  own location families are able to come  here for assistance  no questions asked hope cove is  available for all family dynamics  including single dads grandparents and  foster parents  the nonprofit provides immediate  assistance for items such as diapers  formula hygiene products and more there  are no qualifiers or documents needed to  receive help  people coming from homelessness people  who live in weeklies people who live in  motels  people living with family they just  cannot supply those things  so for those people i founded hope code  eventually dookey would like to move  hope cove to a bigger building and have  multiple locations across the valley  something further south i would like to  have something  in the north end just because a lot of  the people that we serve have no  transportation  dukey even has plans to take hope cove  across state lines to help as many  families as possible kate houston 8 news  now  and she's really made an impact hope  cove has helped more than  2 300 families just since may and right  now the nonprofit though is reliant  solely on donations so here's what they  need  diapers sizes three and up along with  baby wipes and they always need formula  to see how you can donate or perhaps  maybe you need help you can head to our  website at 8newsnow.com
 

